laurel 2901: calendar from the PM6125 RTC, USB settime/time (port of negroni 0203 + 0212).

- bsd/dev/laurel_rtc.c: SweetPlatformExpert::get/setUTCTimeOfDay. PM6125 RTC_RW (SPMI SID 0, peripheral
  0x60, qpnp-rtc: ctrl 0x6046 bit 7, seconds 0x6048..0x604b) read over the arbiter v5 observer channel of
  its APID (trinket bases as laurel 2018), never written (DT qcom,qpnp-rtc-write = <0>). Wall = RTC +
  offset; the offset of the last set (settimeofday / USB settime) is saved in /private/var/db/laurel_rtc
  and applied in bsd_init before launchd. Floor: the kernel build date. One line
  "LAUREL CALENDAR: on: PM6125 RTC ..." or "LAUREL CALENDAR: off: <reason> (...)". Kill switch laurelrtc=0;
  laurelrtcoff=<s> gives the offset.
- IOKitInitializeTime waits (10 s max) for the platform expert, so the calendar is not the epoch.
- Command server: "settime S[.U]" (usblog.sh sends it at every connect) and "time". In raw mode (before the
  ue0 attach) the settime value is kept and set at the attach, plus the time since it came.

